course: dictionary
lesson: 6892
title: Compound words: overtime
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A compound word is two smaller words joined to make one new word. When you spot the two parts, you can often work out what the whole word means. «A compound word joins two words, like butter + fly = butterfly.»
explain: Overtime is made from over and time. «Overtime is working extra hours beyond the normal ones.» So overtime is time worked beyond the usual time. Check it in a sentence: "I did overtime at work" means I worked past my normal hours.
explain: Sometimes overtime is paid at a higher rate, and sometimes it is not paid at all. Words can also stretch to new meanings. "My brain is working overtime" does not mean your brain is extra time: it means it is working very hard.
fact: A compound word is made from two words joined together, such as butterfly or timetable.
fact: «Overtime» means extra time someone works after their normal working hours.
fact: «Overtime» can also mean the money paid for that extra work.
fact: In North American sport, «overtime» is extra time added to the end of a game when the score is tied. In the UK, football calls this extra time.
fact: «Working overtime» is an informal phrase meaning working very hard.
exercise: «Overtime is working extra hours beyond the normal ones.» What is overtime? | *Extra time worked after normal hours | Time off work for a holiday | A clock that shows the time | A game that has been tied
exercise: Overtime is a compound word. Which two smaller words join to make it? | over and team | *over and time | out and time | open and tide
exercise: In North American sport, a game «goes into overtime» when what happens? | A player is injured | *The score is tied | The game starts early | The crowd goes home
test: «Sometimes overtime is paid at a higher rate, sometimes not paid at all.» Besides extra working hours, what else can overtime mean? | A short holiday | A type of sports shoe | A broken clock | *The money paid for that extra work
test: Ella says «My brain is working overtime» means her brain is broken. What does the phrase really mean? | Her brain is full of water | Her brain is asleep | *Her brain is working very hard | Her brain has stopped
exam: Which word is a compound word, and what do its parts mean together? | *timetable: a table of times, showing when things happen | bright: giving out light | happy: full of joy | castle: a big old building
